No, because he allows for 200 in weight units. If he wants 2400
nutrition, in the form of K's or Lembas, that would be somewhere
between 15 weight units (3 lembas wafers) and 60 weight units (6 K's).
That would be entirely reasonable, and even perhaps on the low end of
what I'd suggest.

What he's really allowing for, however, is 8000 nutrition (10 "full
meals") composed of 20 K's, for a total of 200 weight. That, I'd say,
is overkill. (I think what I mean by overkill is, "Fine if it doesn't
make you burdened, but not worth slowing yourself down for." Unless
you're spending entirely too much time duking it out with Famine, I
don't see how anyone could go from satiated to fainting eight times
during the endgame--not counting food available from the Planes
themselves!)

What I was complaining about was that I had to go back to the spoilers
to make the connection between the OP's idiosyncratic term "full meal"
and its connection to the topic at hand, which was the weight of the
AK. I also had to go back to the spoilers for an explanation of why he
considers this a "full meal"; presumably, since there's a 1000 point
differential between fainting and satiation, 800 is a reasonable
amount to eat when you're on the low edge of "hungry" or into "weak",
without satiating yourself.

All of this, of course, ignores the fact that eating monster corpses
is still allowable on the Planes. Incidentally, although I did find a
table listing nutrition values and weights for various monsters, I
didn't find anything that indicated how long it takes to eat various
types of corpses (determined by nutrition value? size? weight?).

