Sigh. How often has that happened to you? Dungeon adventuring is the
business of gamblers. IMO, a good way to get yourself killed is by
burdening yourself with redundant means to deal with every possible
eventuality, no matter how remote.

But, to deal with your example:
1) Teleport the boulder out of the way.
2) Fire rays or missles past the boulder, killing the jelly and
enabling you to push the boulder forward.
3) Have the force bolt spell.
4) As a last desperate measure, wish for your damn pickaxe back.

